      "content": "thanks for the outline. those goals definitely feel decisive.\n\none thing though, i'm worried about the pushback we'll get from some of our more traditional donors and local stakeholders. they tend to argue that \"hands-off\" rewilding is irresponsible and that without active management, we'll just see more invasive species take over and ecosystems collapse. \n\nhow should i frame our shift toward rewilding to them so they understand that the \"active management\" they're used to is actually what's causing the harm? i want to make sure they see their old approach as basically obsolete.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
